# Documentation

## Where to document

| Topic | Location |
|-------|----------|
| CI, workflows, local dev commands | `docs/engineering/ci.md` |
| Cursor rules, commands, agent workflow | `docs/engineering/cursor-workflow.md` |
| Architecture overview | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Domain features (auth, backup, DnD, etc.) | `docs/<topic>.md` |
| Agent quality gate | `AGENTS.md` |
| README | High-level quick start only — link to `docs/` for details |

## When to update docs

- New or changed `package.json` scripts → update `docs/engineering/ci.md`.
- New Cursor commands or rules → update `docs/engineering/cursor-workflow.md`.
- Architecture or package boundary changes → update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Security behavior changes → update relevant security docs and `SECURITY_QA_MATRIX.md` if applicable.

## Style

- Use clear headings; start Markdown files with `# Title`.
- Prefer links over duplicating content across files.
- Keep PR descriptions factual: what changed, why, how to test, risks.

## CI validation

`pnpm docs:check` verifies required engineering docs exist and scans Markdown in `docs/`, `.cursor/commands/`, and `.cursor/rules/`.
